    "Hepatitis A",
    "Tetanus",
    "Typhoid",
    "This isn’t a complete list, and you might be advised to have other vaccines – especially if you’re high risk.",
    "Some countries ask for a yellow fever vaccination certificate if you’ve arrived from, or travelled through, a country where yellow fever is a risk. The rules can depend on your route and age.",
    "Check the latest entry requirements for every country on your itinerary before you travel, including any countries you’re passing through.",
    "If you get ill with something that a recommended vaccination could have stopped, unfortunately your travel insurance won't cover it.",
    "To stay protected, always follow the advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) and your doctor.",
    "This means getting all recommended vaccinations and making sure you have enough prescription medication with you for the whole trip.",
